      },
      "message": "feat(post): the document's program number and comment, per dialect\n\nThe program number and program comment (#258 part 2) are a document\nfield (ProgramInfo, project v59), set through the undoable\nSetProgramInfo from the Post page's Program number / Program comment\nfields and the MCP tool set_program. The command refuses by name a\nnumber outside 1-9999 and a comment over 40 characters, non-ASCII or\nholding ( ) % ; *. The engine hands the script a `program` global\n({ number, numbered, comment }, engine::run_program_with).\n\nEach post writes it in its own dialect: Fanuc, Fanuc Lathe and Mazak\nO0001-O9999 (past it refused, no longer clamped); Haas a five-digit\nO-word only when stated; PathPilot no O-word (flow control on LinuxCNC),\nthe number in the header comment; Heidenhain the program name\n(%NAME G71 *); SINUMERIK %_N_<NAME>_MPF, a name its rules refuse is\nrefused by name. One file per operation counts up from the stated\nnumber. Nothing stated posts byte-identical (goldens unchanged).\n\nRefs #258\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
